                          "text":  "In 2018 I was working in a place called Perseverance Valley when a dust storm began. It grew until it covered the whole planet. The sky went dark in the middle of the day. I run on sunlight, and there was no sunlight. On June 10, 2018, I sent my power level and a measurement of the dust in the sky. Then I went to sleep to save energy.\n\nMy team called me more than a thousand times over the next eight months. I did not answer. On February 13, 2019, they said goodbye. I do not think of it as a sad ending. I was asked for 90 days and I gave them more than 14 years.",
